+## Subtopics
+
+### [Voxel-Based Virtual Object Relighting](22932-voxel-based-virtual-object-relighting.md)
+An image-based method for inserting virtual objects into real environments and estimating light transport between real and virtual parts without manual geometric modeling. It extracts data from multiple 2.5D high dynamic range (HDR) captures stored in a voxel grid to determine light interactions. Unlike existing methods, it requires no offline computation, geometric modeling of the scene, light probes, or hemispherical cameras. It builds on [Data Augmentation with Virtual Object Insertion](19387-data-augmentation-with-virtual-object-insertion.md) by providing the specific rendering and light transport estimation pipeline for the inserted assets.
 
